cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use receipts, please cite it as below."
title: "receipts: claim-level verification of AI coding agent reports"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Raj
    family-names: Kashikar
repository-code: "https://github.com/raj200501/receipts"
url: "https://github.com/raj200501/receipts"
abstract: >-
  receipts splits an AI coding agent's final report into atomic claims, checks each
  one against a hash-chained ledger of what happened in the agent's sandbox (commands,
  exit codes, test runs, diffs, and hidden checks), and labels it supported,
  contradicted, or unverifiable with the evidence attached. It ships a benchmark of
  synthetic repositories with hidden checks, a study design drafted as
  preregistrations, and a
  Claude Code Stop hook that asks the agent to correct a contradicted report.
license: MIT
version: 0.0.1
date-released: 2026-11-25
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - evaluation
  - honesty
  - coding agents
